\section{Finding free time slots}

A working day runs from 08:00 to 17:00.  People book slots in it, and we
want to know which parts of the day are still free.  The program reads
bookings such as [[09:00-10:30]] from standard input, one per line, and
prints the free slots in the same format.

The whole program has four parts, which we meet in this order:
\begin{enumerate}
\item parsing and formatting of times and slots,
\item merging bookings into disjoint busy intervals,
\item taking the complement of the busy intervals within the working day,
\item the command-line entry point that ties them together.
\end{enumerate}
Both output files come from this one source:

